    "answer": {
      "short": "$x+\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{x}{5}=1000$. First-day distance: 438 km, to the nearest kilometre.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the distance travelled on the first day, in kilometres.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{x}{5}&=1000\\\\\\frac{60x}{60}+\\frac{30x}{60}+\\frac{20x}{60}+\\frac{15x}{60}+\\frac{12x}{60}&=1000\\\\\\frac{137x}{60}&=1000\\\\137x&=60000\\\\x&=\\frac{60000}{137}\\\\x&\\approx438\\end{align*}$$\nShe travelled 438 km on the first day, to the nearest kilometre.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
